# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — the knob roster (every knob, its default) and the line grammar; the gate binary at `GATE_SDK_NATIVE_BIN` prints the defaults with `--emit knob-roster`; set only what you override

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — D2's roster: the consumer's own read-only-dispatched agent-type names; default empty (D2 inert) — never a kit-shipped vocabulary (gate-sdk/SPEC.md §The provenance seam)
# DELEGATION_KIT_READONLY_TYPES[] = <agent-type>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The tier binding — the class roster, highest first; default judgment, routing, mechanical, and a value here replaces all three
# DELEGATION_KIT_TIER_CLASSES[] = <class>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The tier binding — one element per class; the model is an alias (follows the newest model) or an exact model id (pinned), the effort optional; default empty (off)
# DELEGATION_KIT_TIER_MODEL[] = judgment=<model>,<effort>
# DELEGATION_KIT_TIER_MODEL[] = mechanical=<model>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The tier binding — a foreign harness's rows in the same grammar, and the harness of each adapter that takes a class; the kit ships neither (each names a vendor), so set both beside the adapters; default empty
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_TIER_MODEL[] = <harness>/<class>=<model>,<effort>
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_HARNESS[] = <adapter>=<harness>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The foreign-vendor run — one `<adapter>=<word>` element per argv word, in order; the kit ships no adapter (each names a vendor's program), so set one in the gitignored `.local` overlay; default empty
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_ADAPTERS[] = <adapter>=<program>
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_ADAPTERS[] = <adapter>=@PROMPT_FILE@

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The foreign-vendor run — an adapter's resume form, one `<adapter>=<word>` element per argv word, restating its confinement, and the literal its session id follows in a turn's output; default empty (every adapter one-shot)
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_RESUME[] = <adapter>=@SESSION_ID@
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_SESSION_MARKER[] = <adapter>=<literal>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The keyed verdict — an adapter's usage snapshot, one per adapter; default empty (the adapter is unbudgeted)
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_USAGE[] = <adapter>=<path>

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The keyed verdict — the argv that writes that snapshot, one `<adapter>=<word>` element per word; the kit ships no producer (each reads a vendor's feed), so set both in the gitignored `.local` overlay; default empty
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_USAGE_CMD[] = <adapter>=<program>
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_USAGE_CMD[] = <adapter>=@USAGE_FILE@

# spec: delegation-kit/SPEC.md §The keyed verdict — the keyed pause thresholds, short window and long; each defaults to the account-keyed knob it derives from
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_PAUSE_PCT = <percent>
# DELEGATION_KIT_FOREIGN_PAUSE_PCT_LONG = <percent>
